VALUES (15188, 'tt0260618', NULL, 'Gardeners'' World', 'Gardeners'' World', 'tv', 1968, 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/dwqMZ7opkE12BmdFkrtwxyvsJl2.jpg', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/bVWXnafKqgwbSWsl0HPKYxMHTK2.jpg', 'Gardeners'' World is a long-running BBC Television programme about gardening, first broadcast in 1968 and still running as of 2013. Its first episode was presented by Ken Burras and came from Oxford Botanical Gardens. The magazine BBC Gardeners'' World is a tie-in to the programme. Most of its episodes have been 30 minutes in length, although there are many specials that last longer. The 2008 and 2009 series used a 60-minute format.', NULL, NULL, 9.9015, 8.2, 0, 1.01, '2026-09-17 03:31:35', '2026-09-17 03:31:35')
